	(text "ALL BUS CAPS ≥100 V, X7R · BULK ELECTROLYTICS ON BUS SHEET"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.594 151.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "02a346f3-f0cb-439a-a164-1f28bd0b85fb")
	)
	(text "GATE DRIVE - IR2184 × 2, one per half-bridge\nOne logic input per half-bridge. The IR2184 generates the complement and enforces\nits own dead time, so sign-magnitude, locked-antiphase and mixed decay are all\nfirmware choices with zero hardware change. Cost: one extra signal per channel.\nBootstrap: +12 V → 1 Ω → ES1D → 1 µF across VB-VS.\n0.41 V droop at 405 nC against a 1.5 V budget → D_max ≈ 94 %.\nSD is ACTIVE LOW (S̄D̄ per datasheet Lead Definitions)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 354.076 153.924 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0ba4bcb2-8341-4a8e-8b43-e8aaf73c65ef")
	)
	(text "ASSUMPTIONS - REV 0, PROVISIONAL\nA1  Coil 2 Ω/coil, 1 Ω/yoke      EDD §2.2 + independent geometry check   UNMEASURED\nA2  Coil 10 mH/coil, k = 0.85    estimate only                           UNMEASURED\nA5  Peak current treated as continuous (deliberately conservative)\nA6  Ambient 40 °C\nA9  60 V is the MAXIMUM bus voltage, not nominal\nA1 is the one that hurts: at 4 Ω the duty goes to 100 % and the bootstrap\nneeds rework. It is also the easiest thing to measure.\nFull register with change costs: levpdu/09_design_sheet_rev0.md §2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 151.638 270.764 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "565af70a-899d-49b4-891e-4b8c894e511f")
	)
	(text "SHEET I/O\nPWM_A, PWM_B   in    one per half-bridge; Schmitt-buffered on IO_PROTECT\nRESET          in    clears the fault latch\nCOIL_A, COIL_B pwr   to the yoke via the barrier strip\nISNS           out   1.65 V ± 20 mV/A\nFAULT          out   HIGH = latched fault\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 153.924 251.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6c0bf757-dd6c-41be-895d-5794aafa480a")
	)
	(text "74HCT132 (Schmitt inputs). Symbol is 74LS132 - library has no HCT variant. Do NOT fit 74LS132 or 74HCT00."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 255.27 48.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8e6e3218-60e3-4dd8-8221-8916231d89d4")
	)
	(text "FAULT LATCH - 74HC74, set-dominant\nWithout a latch an over-current self-clears the instant it trips, and the\nbridge chatters at the trip point.\nFAULT_N → S̄ sets it. Q drives FAULT out; Q̄ drives SD low to shut both\nhalf-bridges down. R18/C22 hold C̄L̄R̄ low at power-up so the latch always comes\nup in the no-fault state. R19 pulls SD low if the latch is unpowered -\nfail-safe direction.\nREV 0 LIMITATION: SD is a hard turn-off, not slow decay. The coil then\nfreewheels into the bus through the body diodes. Safe while the battery is\nconnected; not safe with the bus isolated. Accepted for rev 0 - see\nlevpdu/13_schematic_review_power_channel.md §3.2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 256.54 131.318 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "90feac87-0309-49a5-8970-752538bde705")
	)
	(text "GATE NETWORK - asymmetric on purpose\n10 Ω turning on; 4.7 Ω ∥ 10 Ω ≈ 3.2 Ω turning off. The diode conducts only for\ncurrent leaving the gate, so turn-on speed is untouched.\nWhy: IRF100B201 has C_rss = 310 pF and V_GS(th) = 2.0 V MIN. At 0.54 V/ns the\noff device sees C_rss · dV/dt · R_g = 2.2 V on its own gate through 10 Ω -\nabove threshold. Cutting the off-path to ≈3 Ω gives 1.3 V.\nTurn-on is deliberately left slow: speeding it up would raise dV/dt and make\nthe problem worse.\n10 k pulldowns return to each FET's OWN source, so gates stay defined before\nthe drivers have power."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 319.786 211.328 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "aede147c-bc64-4516-bd67-0428af73add4")
	)
	(text "POWER STAGE - FULL H-BRIDGE\nIRF100B201, 100 V, 4.2 mΩ. 30 A/yoke design current, D ≈ 0.5 at 60 V into ≈1 Ω.\nBidirectional by requirement, not convenience: HEMS force goes as (B_pm ± B_coil)²,\nso the SIGN of coil current changes the force, not just its magnitude.\nQ1/Q3 tabs sit at +60 V, Q2/Q4 tabs at the switch nodes - four different\npotentials, so every device needs an insulating pad to the heatsink."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150.876 202.184 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b88c331b-caf8-4350-810d-c910cfe06657")
	)
	(text "WINDOW COMPARATOR - LM393\nInputs are crossed deliberately: A trips on ISNS > 2.55 V, B trips on\nISNS < 0.75 V, and BOTH pull low. Open-drain outputs tied together give OR.\n1.3 µs propagation delay is not a problem here: worst-case di/dt is 9730 A/s,\nso the current rises 13 mA in that time. The load inductance does the work.\nThe fast fault is shoot-through, and the IR2184's interlock handles that."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.718 85.852 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "dc2090b2-33a2-4754-917d-ae28974864cd")
	)
	(text "BUS DECOUPLING + CLAMP\n8 × 1 µF 1210 + 2 × 100 nF, all ≥100 V X7R, inside the commutation loop.\nBulk electrolytics are on the BUS sheet, shared between both channels -\ninterleaving the two bridges 180° cancels most of the bus ripple, which\nonly helps if the bulk is shared.\nD2 is a residual clamp (113 V at 44 A), not an energy path. Coil energy is\nhandled by slow decay - see FAULT LATCH."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.962 142.494 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e275f710-6ece-4439-bd45-28687c79728c")
	)
	(text "OCP THRESHOLDS\n2.55 V and 0.75 V → ±45 A (30 A legitimate, 60 A ceiling).\nBoth thresholds and the INA240's 1.65 V mid-scale come from the SAME 3V3 rail,\nso the trip point is ratiometric - rail error cancels instead of moving the trip."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.594 18.796 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "efbad297-0012-4ca3-8825-876cfddf9feb")
	)
	(text "CURRENT SENSE - in-line with the coil\n1 mΩ 4-terminal shunt between SW_A and COIL_A. Only this position sees true\nbidirectional coil current; high-side or low-side sensing does not.\nCommon mode is the switch node - a 0-60 V square wave - which is exactly what\nthe INA240 exists for (CMRR 132 dB DC, 93 dB at 50 kHz).\nGain 20 · REF1→GND, REF2→+3V3 gives 1.65 V at zero current · 20 mV/A · ±82 A FS.\nR12/R13 are capped at 10 Ω: anything larger causes gain error against the\namplifier's input impedance.\n4-terminal is mandatory, not preferred - at 1 mΩ the solder joints and pad\ncopper are comparable to the element itself."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.246 93.472 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f4142b2e-1b0c-4ec3-bec9-9d3ef2e0ed20")
	)
